1
00:00:06,680 --> 00:00:08,810
3 quarters of a garden is lawn.

2
00:00:08,860 --> 00:00:13,720
A gardener mows 2 thirds of the lawn before it starts to rain.

3
00:00:13,770 --> 00:00:17,000
What fraction of the whole garden has been mown?

4
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:20,590
Pause the video and work it out.

5
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:24,010
Draw the garden as a rectangle with 4 columns.

6
00:00:24,060 --> 00:00:25,950
3 of the columns are lawn.

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,910
That is 3 quarters.

8
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:30,940
Now cut it into 3 rows, and take 2 of them.

9
00:00:30,990 --> 00:00:33,460
The dark part has been mown.

10
00:00:33,510 --> 00:00:36,620
There are 12 small pieces, and 6 are dark.

11
00:00:36,670 --> 00:00:38,350
6 twelfths is one half.

12
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:41,380
Half of the garden has been mown.

13
00:00:41,430 --> 00:00:44,660
Remember how to find a fraction of an amount.

14
00:00:44,710 --> 00:00:50,900
For 3 fifths of 40, divide by the denominator, then multiply by the numerator.

15
00:00:50,950 --> 00:00:53,130
40 divided by 5 is 8.

16
00:00:53,180 --> 00:00:55,380
8 times 3 is 24.

17
00:00:55,430 --> 00:01:00,860
2 thirds of 3 quarters is the same as 2 thirds times 3 quarters.

18
00:01:00,910 --> 00:01:06,980
To multiply fractions, multiply the numerators, and multiply the denominators.

19
00:01:07,030 --> 00:01:08,220
2 times 3 is 6.

20
00:01:08,270 --> 00:01:09,540
3 times 4 is 12.

21
00:01:09,590 --> 00:01:13,820
That gives 6 twelfths, which simplifies to one half.

22
00:01:13,870 --> 00:01:16,270
It matches the diagram.

23
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:17,000
Your turn.

24
00:01:17,050 --> 00:01:19,430
Work out 1 third times 1 quarter.

25
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:22,810
Pause the video and try it.

26
00:01:22,860 --> 00:01:24,190
1 times 1 is 1.

27
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:25,660
3 times 4 is 12.

28
00:01:25,710 --> 00:01:28,420
The answer is 1 twelfth.

29
00:01:28,470 --> 00:01:32,100
You can make the numbers smaller before you multiply.

30
00:01:32,150 --> 00:01:33,900
This is called cancelling.

31
00:01:33,950 --> 00:01:38,340
Divide a numerator and a denominator by the same number.

32
00:01:38,390 --> 00:01:42,090
In 2 thirds times 3 quarters, the threes cancel.

33
00:01:42,140 --> 00:01:44,360
And 2 and 4 both divide by 2.

34
00:01:44,410 --> 00:01:49,290
That leaves 1 over 1, times 1 over 2, which is one half.

35
00:01:49,340 --> 00:01:53,370
A whole number can be written as a fraction over 1.

36
00:01:53,420 --> 00:01:57,210
So 5 times 2 thirds is 5 over 1, times 2 over 3.

37
00:01:57,260 --> 00:02:00,640
That is 10 thirds, or 3 and 1 third.

38
00:02:00,690 --> 00:02:02,010
Here is the method.

39
00:02:02,060 --> 00:02:06,310
Step 1: write any whole number as a fraction over 1.

40
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:12,170
Step 2: cancel common factors between any numerator and any denominator.

41
00:02:12,220 --> 00:02:17,400
Step 3: multiply the numerators, and multiply the denominators.

42
00:02:17,450 --> 00:02:22,760
Step 4: simplify, and change an improper fraction to a mixed number.

43
00:02:22,810 --> 00:02:26,020
Work out 4 ninths times 3 eighths.

44
00:02:26,070 --> 00:02:27,450
Cancel 4 with 8.

45
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:29,790
They become 1 and 2.

46
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:31,250
Cancel 3 with 9.

47
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:33,630
They become 1 and 3.

48
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:36,760
1 third times 1 half is 1 sixth.

49
00:02:36,810 --> 00:02:39,640
Work out 6 times 5 eighths.

50
00:02:39,690 --> 00:02:41,420
Write 6 as 6 over 1.

51
00:02:41,470 --> 00:02:43,210
Cancel 6 and 8 by 2.

52
00:02:43,260 --> 00:02:45,540
They become 3 and 4.

53
00:02:45,590 --> 00:02:47,140
3 times 5 is 15.

54
00:02:47,190 --> 00:02:48,640
1 times 4 is 4.

55
00:02:48,690 --> 00:02:52,400
15 quarters is 3 and 3 quarters.

56
00:02:52,450 --> 00:02:53,150
Your turn.

57
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:55,090
Work out 4 times 3 tenths.

58
00:02:55,140 --> 00:02:58,130
Pause and work it out.

59
00:02:58,180 --> 00:03:01,310
4 times 3 is 12, so we get 12 tenths.

60
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:06,310
That simplifies to 6 fifths, which is 1 and 1 fifth.

61
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:09,500
In a club, 3 fifths of the members are adults.

62
00:03:09,550 --> 00:03:11,920
5 sixths of the adults play tennis.

63
00:03:11,970 --> 00:03:16,140
What fraction of the club are adults who play tennis?

64
00:03:16,190 --> 00:03:18,310
We need 5 sixths of 3 fifths.

65
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:20,200
Of means multiply.

66
00:03:20,250 --> 00:03:21,440
The fives cancel.

67
00:03:21,490 --> 00:03:23,340
3 and 6 cancel to 1 and 2.

68
00:03:23,390 --> 00:03:25,010
The answer is one half.

69
00:03:25,060 --> 00:03:28,770
Half of the club are adults who play tennis.

70
00:03:28,820 --> 00:03:31,850
Omar works out 2 fifths times 3 quarters.

71
00:03:31,900 --> 00:03:33,900
Which line is wrong?

72
00:03:33,950 --> 00:03:35,020
Line 1 is wrong.

73
00:03:35,070 --> 00:03:37,600
Omar multiplied across the wrong way.

74
00:03:37,650 --> 00:03:41,090
Multiply top by top, and bottom by bottom.

75
00:03:41,140 --> 00:03:44,250
2 times 3 is 6, and 5 times 4 is 20.

76
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:47,970
6 twentieths simplifies to 3 tenths.

77
00:03:48,020 --> 00:03:50,640
Here is a real fraction of a fraction.

78
00:03:50,690 --> 00:03:55,250
About 7 tenths of the Earth's surface is covered by water.

79
00:03:55,300 --> 00:04:00,350
And the Pacific Ocean holds roughly half of all that water surface.

80
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:03,180
One half times 7 tenths is 7 twentieths.

81
00:04:03,230 --> 00:04:08,560
So the Pacific Ocean alone covers about a third of the whole planet.

82
00:04:08,610 --> 00:04:09,880
One last question.

83
00:04:09,930 --> 00:04:14,230
Is 3 quarters times 4 fifths more than 3 quarters, or less?

84
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:17,610
Pause the video and choose.

85
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:19,560
It is less than 3 quarters.

86
00:04:19,610 --> 00:04:24,310
Multiplying by a fraction smaller than 1 makes the answer smaller.

87
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:28,750
In fact, the fours cancel, and the answer is 3 fifths.

88
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:31,570
To remember: of means multiply.

89
00:04:31,620 --> 00:04:36,800
Multiply the numerators, multiply the denominators, and simplify.

90
00:04:36,850 --> 00:04:40,580
Cancel common factors first, to make it easier.

91
00:04:40,630 --> 00:04:42,980
A whole number is a fraction over 1.

92
00:04:43,030 --> 00:04:47,670
And multiplying by a proper fraction makes the answer smaller.

93
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:52,910
Great work! Now practise lesson 7.3 on Camday.
